<witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T00:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T01:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Bled off pressure to 0 bar above DHSV. Confirmed valve status and handed over well to drilling at 01:00.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T01:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T02:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Transferred HMV and DHSV to local controled panel (wireline lock-out mode). Connected Seawell pump and tested line up.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T02:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T03:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Installed test and bleed manifold from moonpool outlet to XMT KWV. Prepared bleed down hose and valves from KWV to closed drain.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T03:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T04:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Flushed lines and attempted to perform line test to 30/200 bar for 5/10 min from cmt unit to KWV through test and bleed manifold. Had 8 bar increase on low pressure test. Investigated situation. Performed &quot;line test&quot; for cmt unit seperatly. Ok. Performed line test to 30/200 bar for 5/10 min from cmt unit to KWV through test and bleed manifold.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T04:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T06:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Opened KWV and attempted test XMT cross. Pressure dropped from 20 to 8 bar while pumping and from 26 bar to 11 bar on second attempt. Checked line-up for leaks. No leaks observed. Opened SV. Flushed through XMT through tree cap needle valve. Closed SV and re-attempted to test XMT cross. Pressure dropped from 30 to 8 bar. Closed LTV1 and performed a second line test to 30 bar/5 min. Ok. Opened LTV1 and re-attempted to test XMT cross without sucess.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T06:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T06:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Closed MMV to establish if it was HMV or PWV that was leaking. Re-attempted to test XMT cross without sucess.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T06:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T09:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Operated and greased up PWV.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T09:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T10:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Verified PWV, SV and HMV were closed.  Leak tested XMT cross to 30/200 bar for 5/10 min using cmt unit and 100% MEG. Had 2.4 bar drop (1.2%)/10 min. Bled off pressure to 0 bar to platform closed drain. Verified no pressure below treee cap and removed same.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T10:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T11:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Held tool box talk for installing WL riser and lubricator and change elevator. Lifted WL riser sections and BOP with Top Drive using double lift arrangement. Lowered and stabbed on to XMT connection.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T11:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T12:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Changed elevators and PU lubricator.

Meanwhile pressure tested shear ram on WL BOP to 30/200 bar for 5/10 min. Ok.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T12:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T13:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Man-rode to turn WL sheave wheel.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T13:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T15:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>MU combination toolstring in riser and stabbed on lubricator with in-situ sub.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T15:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T16:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Verified that toolstring was sitting in toolcatcher. Opened SV 10 turns and opened KWV. Filled riser with 100% MEG from cmt unit. Leak tested WL riser, BOP and lubricator to 30/200 bar for 5/10 min using cmt unit and 100% MEG. Ok. Bled off pressure to 0 bar. Closed SV and KWV.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T16:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T16:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- rig up/down</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Performed well control exercise with Seawell, Schlumberger and Mærsk crew.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T16:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T18:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">0</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Opened HMV, KWV and SV 10 turns. Filled well above DHSV with 7.7 m3 100% MEG. Equalized and opened DHSV at 93 bar. Closed KWV and bled off pressureto 0 bar in manifold.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T18:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T19:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">485</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Opened SV with 45 turns. RIH with combination toolstring on 7/16&quot; EWLL to 485 m and took pick up weight.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T19:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T19:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">498</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Attempted to RIH through DHSV, but found solid hold up depth at 498 m.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T19:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T20:45:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">485</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Changed out MEG tanks and re-filled MEG on cmt unit.

Meanwhile held tool box talk prior to equalizing and opening DHSV. Performed well control exercise with Seawell, Schlumberger and Mærsk crew.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T20:45:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T21:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">485</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Opened LTV1 and LTV2. Equalized pressure to 90 bar and opened KWV. Pumped 8.95 m3 100% MEG into well and observed pressure drop from 90 to 69 bar. This confirmed that DHSV was open/partly open.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T21:30:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-14T23:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">485</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Attempted to RIH through DHSV, but found solid hold up depth at 498 m. Discussed further options.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity><witsml:activity><witsml:dTimStart>2009-03-14T23:15:00+01:00</witsml:dTimStart><witsml:dTimEnd>2009-03-15T00:00:00+01:00</witsml:dTimEnd><witsml:md uom="m">485</witsml:md><witsml:phase>wire line</witsml:phase><witsml:proprietaryCode>workover -- wire line</witsml:proprietaryCode><witsml:state>ok</witsml:state><witsml:stateDetailActivity>success</witsml:stateDetailActivity><witsml:comments>Functioned DHSV closed/open twice to remove possible debris. Had 3.0 dl return when closing DHSV and pumped 4.25 dl when opening DHSV. Had good indication of DHSV being in open position.</witsml:comments></witsml:activity>
</witsml:drillReport>
